.TH "HTMLTEMPLATEELEMENT.SHADOWROOTSLOTASSIGNMENT" "3JS" "July 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTemplateElement.shadowRootSlotAssignment \- HTMLTemplateElement:
shadowRootSlotAssignment property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]shadowRootSlotAssignment\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]HTMLTemplateElement\f[R] interface indicates whether the element
has been configured to use named or unnamed slot assignment.
.PP
This property can be used to detect support for the declarative
attribute on the \f[CR]<template>\f[R] element.
.PP
The property can\(cqt be read to determine the slot assignment method of
a shadow root.
This is because a \f[CR]<template>\f[R] element declaration results in
the creation of either an \f[CR]HTMLTemplateElement\f[R] or a
\f[CR]ShadowRoot\f[R].
If a shadow root is created, then the \f[CR]HTMLTemplateElement\f[R]
does not, so you can\(cqt use it to check the slot assignment.
If a \f[CR]HTMLTemplateElement\f[R] is created then it isn\(cqt a shadow
root, and it can\(cqt easily be changed into one \- so the value is
irrelevant
.PP
If defined, it reflects the value of the
\f[CR]shadowrootslotassignment\f[R] attribute of the associated
\f[CR]<template>\f[R] element.
.SH VALUE
A string that reflects the value of the
\f[CR]shadowrootslotassignment\f[R] attribute of the associated
\f[CR]<template>\f[R] element.
Possible values are \f[CR]\(dqnamed\(dq\f[R] and
\f[CR]\(dqmanual\(dq\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Feature detection for \f[CR]shadowrootslotassignment\f[R]
If you\(cqre declaratively creating shadow roots that rely on unnamed
slot assignment, using \f[CR]<template>\f[R] elements, you can use the
existence of this property on the \f[CR]HTMLTemplateElement\f[R] to
feature check for support.
This works because the property was added as the same time as unnamed
assignment using the \f[CR]\(dqmanual\(dq\f[R] value.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] isShadowRootSlotAssignmentSupported = Object.hasOwn(
  HTMLTemplateElement.prototype,
  \(dqshadowRootSlotAssignment\(dq,
);
.EE
.PP
The value of \f[CR]isShadowRootSlotAssignmentSupported\f[R] could then
be used to fallback to attaching the shadow root with
\f[CR]Element.attachShadow()\f[R], or to inform the user of what browser
versions they need to use.
.PP
Note that if you\(cqre using named slot assignment there is no need to
feature check for \f[CR]shadowrootslotassignment\f[R], because named
assignment is supported by default.
.SH SEE ALSO
